      "doctor_question": "Do you hear this man's voice even during times when you are not feeling down or depressed?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_3",
      "patient_response": "Oh, um... well, I don't want to make a big deal out of it, and I really hope you don't think I'm completely losing my mind or anything. \n\nBut, yes... even when I'm not feeling so heavy and sad, and even when I'm not feeling... well, sometimes I get real energetic, too... but even during the calm weeks, when I'm just feeling normal, the voice is still there. \n\nThere was a stretch recently, maybe for a little over two weeks, where my mood was just fine. I was going to work, doing my job, not too high, not too low. But I still heard the man in the vents telling me things. And... well, I also still felt like the people working in the offices were leaving little signs or signals about me when I went in to empty their trash. \n\nI know it sounds bad, and I really try not to let it bother me or get in the way of my cleaning. I just try to keep my head down. Does that make sense, Doctor? I hope I'm not making things too complicated.",
